cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'IoT and Smart Home Security — T39'
message: >-
  If you use or reference this work, please cite it using
  the metadata from this file.
type: software
version: '1.0.1'
date-released: '2026-09-24'
abstract: >-
  A study of IoT and smart-home security, focusing on Wi-Fi sensing
  countermeasures (WiShield, ACSAC 2024) and automated wireless
  protocol fuzzing for IoT bug reproduction (AirBugCatcher, ACSAC
  2024). Produced as Data and Network Security (T39) coursework at
  Sapienza University of Rome, MSc in Cybersecurity. Comprises a
  presentation, a ten-page IEEEtran report on a future research
  direction, and a reproducible reference implementation (RDD, the
  Robust Delta-Debugging tool) with its benchmark suite.
